<title>FRANCE: Schneider rises on buy note.</title>
<headline>Schneider rises on buy note.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in electrical equipment company Schneider rose 1.16 percent to 161.30 francs at 1040 GMT, after Leven put out a buy note, market sources said.</p>
<p>The French brokerage, which hosted a breakfast meeting with the company today, believes the stock is undervalued, particularly since the sale of Spie Batignolles which gives a clearer view of the group.</p>
<p>Moody's upgraded Schneider's senior debt rating earlier this week, which helped stir buying interest in the stock.</p>
